00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.379 align:start position:0%
controlling an autonomous vehicle in  order to accomplish a task requires an  understanding of many aspects of the  problem from the vehicles dynamics to  obstacles to avoid to the values of each  objective it can be inefficient  error-prone or impossible for human  operators to specify a detailed action  sequence thus it is important to elevate  the level of commanding such that human  operators only need to specify a set of  goals to be accomplished and then have  planners produce a series of actions  that achieve the mission goals based on  the model of the physical plant under  control the environment and the  objectives the planner integration  project combines the capabilities of two  planners to provide a robust planning  framework we demonstrate the  integrations capabilities on Odyssey for  an autonomous underwater vehicle or a UV  designed and built by the MIT a UV lab  at Sea Grant the auv has an ability to  dive ascend and glide as well as to take  pictures and CTD readings we can specify  a set of tasks for the auv to complete  the interface allows us to place start  and finish locations manipulate  obstacles place waypoints and enable  discrete actions such as taking a  picture or recording video here a user  is creating a simple task involving  three waypoints surrounding an obstacle  after setting the starting point the  user specifies the desired Waypoint  surrounding the obstacle and also moves  the goal point to the desired location  the yellow edges between the nodes  represent the high-level plan designed  by the operator which crosses an  obstacle in its way Kirk calculates the  first layer of the plan to go around the  obstacle shown here as the green path  finally the red path shows the complete  plan which is the result of calming  refinement the auv executed the plan  successfully in open water the final  trajectory shows the initial movement of  the auv to the start followed by the way  the artifacts from the control as a more  difficult task the auv was tasked with  drawing AK in the ocean the  v executed the plan successfully in open  water the actual trajectory is plotted  in Google Earth the planner integration  project shows not only the successful  integration of Kirk and cong ming but  their interoperation with a vehicle in a  real-world environment
 

